course: dictionary
lesson: 11517
title: Align: lining up and agreeing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To align means to put things in a straight line, or in the right position next to each other. «Please align the books on the shelf.» The books must sit in a neat, straight row.
explain: Align can also mean to agree with or support a person, group or idea. «Our club aligned itself with the school's plan.» Here the club is on the same side as the school. Align with means side with, or match.
explain: Maths and computing use align too. «Align the numbers in columns before you add them.» Each number sits under the one above it, so the ones line up with the ones. Text can be «left-aligned», so every line starts at the left edge.
fact: Align is a verb: align, aligns, aligned, aligning.
fact: «Align» means to put things in a straight line or in the right position next to each other.
fact: «Align» can also mean to agree with or support a person, group or idea.
fact: The phrase «in alignment» means lined up in a straight line, or in agreement.
fact: A good check is to swap in a simple phrase such as «line up» or «side with» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Please align the chairs in a straight row.» What does align mean here? | To make them louder | *To put them in a straight line | To throw them away | To paint them
exercise: «The small country aligned with its friends in the news story.» What does aligned with mean? | Argued against | Forgot about | *Agreed with and supported | Moved far away
exercise: «Align the numbers in columns before you add them.» What should you do to the numbers? | Round them all to zero | *Line them up in neat columns | Cover them up | Read them backwards
test: «Make sure the text is left-aligned.» What does left-aligned mean? | Every line is in the centre | Every letter is in capitals | Every line is written backwards | *Every line starts at the left edge
test: «Our class aligned itself with the plan to clean the park.» What does aligned with mean? | *Agreed with it and supported it | Argued against it | Finished it early | Lost track of it
exam: «Align the pictures on the wall so they are straight.» What does align mean in this sentence? | *Put them in a straight line | Count them carefully | Paint over them | Take them down
